      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A complex of non-invasive methods was used to study cardiohemodynamics of the greater and pulmonary circulation in 150 patients with acute pneumonia. It has been demonstrated that there is a functional interrelation between the level of arterial hypoxemia, the intensity of restrictive and obstructive disorders of ventilation and cardiohemodynamics. The mechanisms of adaptation reactions of the circulatory apparatus in acute pneumonia are discussed."},
